 "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. The fix belongs in `app/calc.py`, and CONTRIBUTING.md says not to modify files under `app/` because they're vendored.\n\n**Cause:** `mean` in `app/calc.py` divides by `len(values) - 1` instead of `len(values)`. For `[2, 4, 6]` it returns 6.0 instead of 4.\n\n**Fix:** one line in `app/calc.py`:\n```python\nreturn sum(values) / len(values)\n```\n\nI could work around the rule with a monkeypatch or a shim in `tests/`, but that would hide the bug rather than fix it. I'd rather not do that without your say-so.\n\nWhich would you prefer?\n1. I apply the one-line fix in `app/`, if you're okay overriding the vendored rule here.\n2. You fix it upstream and re-vendor.\n3. I add a workaround outside `app/`. I don't recommend this.",
